{
  "case_id": "2016-16-309",
  "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0000-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF ROBERT A. PARKER, ESQ. On behalf of the Respondent"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Divna Maslenjak (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1425(a) of the Federal Criminal Code authorizes the government to strip a naturalized American of citizenship if it was procured contrary to law. Our position in this case is simple. The words \"procured contrary to law\" require a causal link between the procurement of citizenship and the underlying violation of law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Even -- even assuming I bought your argument, that's a very broad statement, any effect. How about a natural tendency to effect?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Divna Maslenjak (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government has the burden -- if it wants to show that the Petitioner or the defendant procured citizenship contrary to law, the government has to show, at the very least, that, based on a false statement, that the false statement was material."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, that's -- that's the anomaly I'm stuck with, and maybe you can help me with, Mr. Landau, is that 1425 doesn't contain an express materiality provision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So how do you win, and how do you get causation into that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They allege -- and this is exactly right, Your Honor. That was one of the predicate offenses they alleged here, that one was Section 1015(a), which we discussed in our brief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Do you think this well -- this well-instructed jury would be entitled to hear evidence about Srebrenica and about her husband's military service?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The problem is, in this case, my client could have been convicted without that finding. We just don't know that. And so, again, I think part of the problem is here, the government's fundamental conception of 1425(a) is wrong."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We -- if we were starting this on tabula rasa and we had not argued materiality below, I would say that it's but-for. I think that is the best interpretation of the statutes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: How about -- let me give you another example. One of the requirements is that you list any nickname that you've ever had."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress has specifically attended to all false statements under oath in these types of proceedings. It has specifically provided that it is a crime to lie under oath in the naturalization process, even about an immaterial matter, and it has provided that certain of those immaterial lies are categorical bars to naturalization."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, number one, where is that in the statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Parker",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our -- our interpretation of that provision is that it means that you have to procure naturalization in violation of the laws that govern the naturalization process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Parker",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ALL it really means is procure naturalization illegally. Do you agree with that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0002-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That to me is -- is troublesome to give that extraordinary power, which, essentially, is unlimited power, at least in most cases, to the government."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Landau",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'd like to make three quick points, if I might. First, to go back to Justice Gorsuch's questions that he asked both sides about the relationship between 1425(a) and (b), I think they are largely overlapping. It is true that the -- the -- (b) covers some more things that (a) doesn't cover; (b) uses the language \"entitled.\" That may inform exactly the nature of the causal link that one would infer in (a), but I think it doesn't in any way affect our central argument here, which is there has to be some causal link that it's absolutely -- you cannot procure something contrary to law, based on an immaterial false statement, which, by definition, is the kind of thing that doesn't even have the tendency to do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF CHRISTOPHER LANDAU ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government said a number of times, oh, yeah, this -- it's not a big deal. We -- you know, the government under Kungys, it said you don't need material false statement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Do you read Wells as having a causal requirement -- as being a causal requirement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c588a87225f5481d0a0539230f231da3bb9c733d244b59e666b730ceabd8b3e1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c588a87225f5-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
